@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@kcUrl = http://localhost:8080/realms/medicitas/protocol/openid-connect/token
@password = Medicitas123!

### 1. Obtener token de Recepcion (Clinica 1)
# @name loginRecep
POST {{kcUrl}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=medicitas-api&username=recep1a&password={{password}}

### 2. Obtener token de Profesional (Clinica 1)
# @name loginProf
POST {{kcUrl}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=medicitas-api&username=prof1a&password={{password}}

### 3. Obtener token de Admin Clinica (Clinica 1)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{kcUrl}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=medicitas-api&username=admin1&password={{password}}

### 4. Obtener token de Admin Clinica 2 (para prueba de aislamiento I5)
# @name loginAdmin2
POST {{kcUrl}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=medicitas-api&username=admin2&password={{password}}

@tokenRecep = {{loginRecep.response.body.access_token}}
@tokenProf = {{loginProf.response.body.access_token}}
@tokenAdmin = {{loginAdmin.response.body.access_token}}
@tokenAdmin2 = {{loginAdmin2.response.body.access_token}}

### 5. RF7: Consultar disponibilidad (1ra vez MISS en PostgreSQL, 2da vez HIT en Redis)
GET {{baseUrl}}/profesionales/1/disponibilidad?fecha=2026-12-10&servicio_id=1
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRecep}}

### 6. RF9: Reservar cita (201 Created e invalida cache en Redis)
# @name crearCita
POST {{baseUrl}}/citas
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRecep}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "paciente_id": 1,
  "profesional_id": 1,
  "servicio_id": 1,
  "inicio": "2026-12-10T09:00:00-06:00"
}

### 7. I1: Intentar reservar el mismo espacio (debe responder 409 ESPACIO_TOMADO)
POST {{baseUrl}}/citas
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRecep}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "paciente_id": 2,
  "profesional_id": 1,
  "servicio_id": 1,
  "inicio": "2026-12-10T09:00:00-06:00"
}

### 8. I5: Intentar leer cita de Clinica 1 usando token de Clinica 2 (debe responder 404)
@citaId = {{crearCita.response.body.cita_id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/citas/{{citaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin2}}

### 9. RF17: Intentar consultar bitacora como Recepcion (debe responder 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bitacora
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRecep}}

### 10. RF19: Consultar bitacora de auditoria como Admin Clinica (200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bitacora?paciente_id=1
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}